GUI scripts for Dungeons of Ethren (GameType ethren, DCC rules).

ethren starts from the demo's GUI. GUIScript.cpp puts this directory first on
the Python path and GUIScripts/demo right after it, so every module not found
here comes from the demo (and then from the shared GUIScripts/). To change one
of the demo's screens, copy that module here and edit the copy. New ethren-only
screens (funnel, DCC record sheet, level-up) also go here.

GameCheck.IsGemRBDemo () is true for ethren as well, since the shared scripts
use it to pick the demo's window layouts; use GameCheck.IsEthren () for
anything that should differ from the demo.

Modules here so far:
- MessageWindow.py: the demo's, plus an "R" button for the record screen, the
  party roster and the dcctest and funneltest autotest hooks.
- GUIREC.py: the DCC record screen, plain text in a window built from code.
- DCCSheet.py: formats GemRB.GetDCCStats for the record screen and logs.
- DCCLuck.py: the record screen's Luck panel (burn policy, the Luck to keep,
  pause on key rolls, halflings burning for allies) and Deeds panel (signature
  deed, a one-off for the next attack), M2.4; the Combat panel (charge or
  grapple for the next melee attack, subdual blows, battle rage), M2.3b.
- GUIREC.py also has the "Roll body over" button (GemRB.DCCRecoverBody), M2.3b.
- DCCMagic.py: the spellbook window (M2.5) from the record screen's "Spells":
  known spells (greyed while lost, pressing one casts it), the spellburn and
  corruption Luck settings, and for clerics atonement, lay on hands and turn
  unholy; plus the record sheet's magic lines.
- DCCAutotest.py: the DCC checks of testdata/dcctest's autotest; idle unless
  the DCC_AUTOTEST global is 1.
- Roster.py (M2.9): the party roster for up to 16 (the funnel), since the demo
  GUI has no portrait window: two columns of eight on the right edge, a click
  selects one, a right click adds or removes one, plus everyone, the formation
  and the party settings. Refreshes on a timer.
- DCCParty.py (M2.9): the party settings: Luck policy, pause on key rolls,
  spellburn and corruption Luck for every character this player controls, and
  the host's prompt options (auto-resolve after N seconds, level-0 prompts).
- DCCLearn.py (M2.9): the learn window after a level-up: the new spells, swaps
  where the rules allow (clerics choose; wizards and elves up to half), the
  elf's lucky spell, the notes on rows without content, confirm. Opened from
  the spellbook's "New spells..." button.
- FunnelAutotest.py (M2.9): the checks of testdata/funneltest's autotest; idle
  unless the FNT_AUTOTEST global is 1.
